269
00:19:19,144 --> 00:19:22,624
I've heard it said that all men have some sort of dangerous cootie virus.

270
00:19:23,124 --> 00:19:25,484
Is that what caused you to grow so fat all of a sudden?

271
00:19:25,984 --> 00:19:28,524
I hate to break it to you, but I don't think cooties are real,

272
00:19:28,764 --> 00:19:30,644
and the fat thing is kind of hard to explain,

273
00:19:30,744 --> 00:19:32,684
so let's just say that yeah, all guys turn fat.

274
00:19:33,264 --> 00:19:36,804
Anyway, there was something I left in the pocket of my old pair of pants.

275
00:19:37,264 --> 00:19:38,264
Do you still have it?

276
00:19:39,244 --> 00:19:41,024
Because it's super important to me.

277
00:19:42,544 --> 00:19:46,704
Let me see.

278
00:19:47,204 --> 00:19:48,504
Is this what you mean?

279
00:19:50,664 --> 00:19:51,184
Yes!

280
00:19:51,404 --> 00:19:51,884
Yes!

281
00:19:52,184 --> 00:19:53,604
Man, I was so worried!

282
00:19:54,004 --> 00:19:56,364
I don't know what I would have done if I'd lost it!

283
00:19:56,364 --> 00:20:01,224
Thank you!

284
00:20:01,404 --> 00:20:02,644
You're a real lifesaver!

285
00:20:04,724 --> 00:20:06,304
Get your hands off me!

286
00:20:08,824 --> 00:20:09,744
Stay put.

287
00:20:09,924 --> 00:20:10,644
You're mine.

288
00:20:11,024 --> 00:20:12,104
Something was written on it,

289
00:20:12,184 --> 00:20:13,624
so I kept it just in case.

290
00:20:13,624 --> 00:20:22,064
So, what is it for?

291
00:20:22,584 --> 00:20:23,644
Here, look.

292
00:20:27,484 --> 00:20:28,524
How unusual.

293
00:20:28,864 --> 00:20:30,124
It looks like it's moving.

294
00:20:30,124 --> 00:20:37,784
A bunch of stuff happened,

295
00:20:38,084 --> 00:20:41,624
and then all my friends went flying through the air in different directions.

296
00:20:41,624 --> 00:20:47,044
But now, with this piece of paper,

297
00:20:47,244 --> 00:20:49,684
I can find my way back to them wherever they go.

298
00:20:52,484 --> 00:20:54,224
They're strong, so I'm not worried.

299
00:20:55,884 --> 00:20:58,204
Anyway, guess I should pay you back for all your help.

300
00:20:58,464 --> 00:21:00,664
If there's anything I can do for you, just ask.

301
00:21:00,664 --> 00:21:02,224
Oh, there is!

302
00:21:02,424 --> 00:21:04,504
Could you take out your family jewels so I can see them?

303
00:21:04,704 --> 00:21:05,804
That's not even funny!

304
00:21:05,884 --> 00:21:06,924
You're gonna kill me!

305
00:21:07,404 --> 00:21:09,984
Men are savages and cheapskates.

306
00:21:10,044 --> 00:21:12,804
Just put the sword down and leave my jewels alone, please!

307
00:21:13,504 --> 00:21:15,884
These friends of yours, who are they exactly?

308
00:21:16,224 --> 00:21:16,564
Ugh.

309
00:21:17,124 --> 00:21:18,404
Well, we're all a pirate crew.

310
00:21:19,104 --> 00:21:20,464
Do you know what pirates are here?

311
00:21:21,184 --> 00:21:22,484
Yes, of course I know.

312
00:21:22,904 --> 00:21:25,884
In fact, the empress of this country is a pirate as well.

313
00:21:26,204 --> 00:21:27,064
Oh, really?

314
00:21:27,564 --> 00:21:30,244
So, you guys have, like, an all-girl pirate crew?

315
00:21:31,084 --> 00:21:32,264
Are they strong?

316
00:21:32,704 --> 00:21:34,464
What a foolish question.

317
00:21:38,124 --> 00:21:42,804
Only the most elite warriors are allowed to ride aboard the pirate ship of our empress.

318
00:21:43,904 --> 00:21:45,864
So, yes, of course they're strong.

319
00:21:50,964 --> 00:21:55,104
In this proud nation, all of the women look up to the snake princess.

320
00:21:55,884 --> 00:21:57,444
Her beauty is unparalleled.

321
00:21:57,824 --> 00:21:59,084
She's strong and noble.

322
00:21:59,084 --> 00:22:02,504
She's called the pirate empress, Boa Hancock.

323
00:22:03,384 --> 00:22:05,784
She and her sisters are the protectors of this island.

324
00:22:06,264 --> 00:22:09,444
And, well, truth be told, they're our heroes.

325
00:22:09,444 --> 00:22:25,444
Oh, no, the ship of the snake princess is nearly here!

326
00:22:25,444 --> 00:22:25,664
Huh?

327
00:22:25,664 --> 00:22:26,424
Curse.

328
00:22:32,524 --> 00:22:33,004
What?

329
00:22:33,344 --> 00:22:33,424
Curse.

330
00:22:33,604 --> 00:22:34,724
This isn't good.

331
00:22:34,944 --> 00:22:36,484
We must deal with the man quickly.

332
00:22:36,484 --> 00:22:43,484
Kikyo! He jumped over the wall and disappeared! What should we do now?

333
00:22:43,484 --> 00:22:46,484
Warriors! To the jungle!

334
00:22:46,484 --> 00:22:51,484
We will rescue Margaret, then put the man to death!

335
00:22:51,484 --> 00:22:54,484
The Snake Princess has returned!

336
00:23:06,484 --> 00:23:12,484
Navy Vice Admiral Momonga contacts the Kuja Pirates with an official summons for Boa Hancock.

337
00:23:12,484 --> 00:23:21,484
However, despite being one of the warlords of the sea, Hancock refuses the Navy's request and unleashes her devil fruit power on the unsuspecting Marines.

338
00:23:21,484 --> 00:23:29,484
On the next One Piece, everyone falls in love with Pirate Empress Hancock! I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

